  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Several volunteers know the agreed seedling routine, and a roster can cover short care periods.\", \"decision\": \"How should volunteers choose who tends young seedlings?\", \"goal\": \"Keep routine garden work visible and shared without requiring everyone to attend at the same time.\", \"problem\": \"A small community garden has established beds, safe shared tools, a water supply, and volunteers whose availability varies. Gardening methods are already agreed; the new work is organizing participation, observations, and shared resources. Each decision below covers a distinct coordination need and can be combined with any choices at the other decisions.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nVolunteers choose seedling care periods on the roster, and the coordinator fills any gaps afterward. Most care periods follow volunteered availability.\nThe coordinator assigns seedling care periods on the roster, and volunteers swap periods as needed. Every period has an initial owner before adjustments.\nPairs of volunteers choose neighboring seedling care periods and enter both names on the roster. Each handover has a familiar partner on the next period."
    }
